---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Calculator from '../components/Calculator.astro';
---
<Shell title="Peptide dose-to-volume calculator" description="Convert your specified mg or mcg dose and mg/mL concentration into mL, with an optional clearly labeled U-100 syringe scale." active="/calculator">
  <div class="page-heading"><h1>Dose to volume calculator</h1><p>Use a target dose and concentration you have independently verified.</p></div>
  <Calculator />
  <section class="prose explanation"><h2>How the arithmetic works</h2><p>Convert mcg to mg by dividing by 1,000. Divide the resulting mg by the concentration in mg/mL to obtain mL. For an explicitly selected U-100 syringe, multiply mL by 100 to obtain scale markings.</p><p>International Units (IU) express biological activity for specific substances. This tool does not convert peptide mass to IU. It does not calculate a dose from body weight, infer concentration from a product name, or round a result to a usable injection.</p><p>Unit confusion can cause serious dosing errors. See the <a href="https://www.fda.gov/drugs/human-drug-compounding/fda-alerts-health-care-providers-compounders-and-patients-dosing-errors-associated-compounded" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">FDA explanation of dose, volume and syringe-unit errors</a>.</p></section>
</Shell>
